    "submission": "submission-explained-explore.json",
    "summary": "Turn 10 explained the executed exploration and fixed the next discriminator; no map object was changed (map basis stays at v4).\n\nThe trusted runner executed the harness from the previous turn in a clean copy (check 60f600bb17a047a5807e4dc72a5cd89c, exit 0) and reproduced the local construction events exactly: recovery_seed with seed_lb_ballot -1, record_vbal_reported_by_self 3 and instance_vbal_after_seed 3 with self_status NONE; the peer's real PrepareReply delivered (prepare_replies 2); resolution with lb_status PREACCEPTED, instance status PREACCEPTED, one NOOP command stored, adopted_committed_vector false, and a PreAccept emitted (out code 11); and the final event showing remote status COMMITTED but the instance left PREACCEPTED with command NONE. So the mechanism is real in the delivered code: a recovering replica holding only a default record ignores a reply that reports the instance already COMMITTED at an older vbal and restarts phase 1 with NOOP.\n\nWhat this does and does not establish. It is construction knowledge, not property Evidence: no obligation is fixed, the peer's COMMITTED record was prepared directly rather than produced by a proposal/accept/commit round, and the recovering replica's record was a default. The product states that explicitly rather than promoting the observation.\n\nNext discriminators (recorded in feedback and in the active Candidate's unknowns). First, whether the ignored COMMITTED reply also prevents recovery from ever finishing: the accept phase the recoverer enters needs a majority of acceptOKs, while handleAccept on an already-COMMITTED record refuses to store the new attributes and answers with its own bal, which handleAcceptReply drops via the lastTriedBallot check. Second, whether the consequence is therefore a permanently blocked row and frozen catch-up at the recovering replica rather than two divergent committed vectors, which decides whether importance is progress or agreement. Third, whether a full legal history (real proposal, accept round, commit broadcast, execution timeout) reaches the same state, which is what a formal check must fix as its requirement, applicability and oracle. The accept-status premise remains open as its own question."
